# verified via `gh api repos/.../branches/main/protection`). The real enforcement is GitHub's refusal
# of same-account self-approval: a PR author can never approve their own PR, which is what makes the
# pr-brain/pr-adversary draft→ready transition a meaningful pass signal instead of a formality.
# Claude may approve and merge to `main` autonomously per CLAUDE.md's 2026-08-01 "Claude may merge to
# main itself" directive — that authority is not gated by this file.
# Cloud agents and CI open PRs to `beta`; only the founder promotes `beta → main`.
# (The former `stable` tier was retired — production is two-stage: feat/* → beta → main. See ADR-045.)

